    "modelAnswer": "The enjoyable evening I want to describe happened last autumn, on a cool Saturday night. I spent that night with three of my closest university friends at a rented small apartment, where we held a casual get-together. None of us had heavy study deadlines that weekend, so we could fully relax. We took turns preparing simple home-cooked dishes and ordered some tasty take-out food. After dinner, we sat on the floor, played light-hearted board games and shared interesting stories from our campus life. We chatted freely about our worries, small dreams and funny little incidents that had happened recently. We did not go to noisy bars or crowded entertainment venues. All the happiness came from sincere conversation and comfortable company. What made this evening so special was the relaxed atmosphere. There was no pressure to perform or keep up appearances. We could just be our true selves around each other. Those warm moments created precious memories, and I still look back on that night with great fondness.",
    "modelAnswerZh": "我想描述的愉快夜晚发生在去年秋天，一个凉爽的周六晚上。我和三位大学里最要好的朋友，在一间短租小公寓聚会。那个周末我们都没有紧迫的学业截止任务，可以彻底放松。我们轮流做简单家常菜，也点了好吃的外卖。晚饭过后，我们席地而坐，玩轻松的桌游，互相分享校园生活里的趣事。我们无拘无束聊起各自的烦恼、小小的理想，还有最近发生的各种搞笑小事。我们没有去喧闹酒吧或者人挤人的娱乐场所，全部的快乐都来自真诚交谈与舒服的陪伴。这个夜晚格外珍贵，在于氛围十分松弛。不需要刻意伪装，不用顾及体面，我们可以在彼此面前做最真实的自己。那些温暖片段构成珍贵回忆，直到现在回想起来，我依旧十分怀念那个夜晚。",
    "part3": [
      {
        "q": "Q1. What are the differences between young people's leisure time activities and those of old people?",
        "a": "Young people and the elderly tend to choose quite different leisure activities. Young generations prefer social gatherings, online entertainment and outdoor adventurous activities. They pursue excitement and novelty in their spare hours. In contrast, older people favour slower-paced pastimes such as gardening, walking and watching traditional television programs. Their activities focus more on relaxation rather than new stimulation. Of course, individual personal hobbies can break these general patterns.",
        "zh": "年轻人和老年人选择的休闲活动往往差别很大。年轻人更喜欢聚会、线上娱乐、户外有挑战性的活动，闲暇时光追求新鲜感与刺激。与之相比，老年人偏爱节奏舒缓的消遣，例如养花、散步、看传统电视节目，活动重心更多放在放松身心，而非寻求新鲜刺激。当然，个人爱好也会打破这种普遍规律。"
      },
      {
        "q": "Q2. What can we do to bring family members closer together?",
        "a": "Several practical ways can strengthen bonds among family members. Setting aside regular family time for shared meals or short outings is really helpful. During this time, people should reduce phone-screen distractions and have face-to-face conversations. In addition, family members can take part in simple group tasks together, such as cooking or housework. Mutual respect and patient listening, more than expensive gifts, build genuine family closeness.",
        "zh": "有不少切实可行的办法拉近家庭成员之间的距离。留出固定家庭时间，一起吃饭或者短途出游很有帮助。相处的时候少看手机，进行面对面交流。除此之外家人可以共同完成简单集体任务，比如做饭做家务。比起贵重礼物，互相尊重和耐心倾听，才可以建立真正紧密的亲情。"
      },
      {
        "q": "Q3. How do people get along in a big family?",
        "a": "Getting along well in a large extended family requires tolerance and mutual understanding. Different generations hold varied viewpoints on many issues, so people need to avoid forcing their own opinions onto others. It is unrealistic for every family member to agree all the time. Keeping appropriate personal boundaries and showing respect can reduce conflicts. Small acts of care also help maintain harmonious relationships within big families.",
        "zh": "在大家庭中和睦相处，需要包容和互相体谅。不同代际看待很多问题观念不一样，不要把自己想法强加给别人。要求所有人时时刻刻意见完全一致并不现实。保持恰当边界，互相尊重，就可以减少矛盾。一些小小的关心举动，也有助于维系大家庭内部的和谐。"
      }
    ]
